    "text": "An object diagram of an example regulation. The central Regulation box lists: spdxId: ExampleID1234567890; description: an Example for a export Regulation; creationInfo: CreationInfo[1]; externalRef: ExternalRef[0..*]; comment: xsd:string[0..1]; summary: 2025 export Regulation for \"XYZ\"; name: DIN 123456789. An arrow runs from Regulation to CreationInfo (specVersion: 3.1; created: 2025 08 31; createdBy:; createdUsing: Tool[0..*]; comment: xsd:string[0..1]), and from CreationInfo to Organization (description: Government Organization; name: Gov Org; spdxId: Org1abcd). Another arrow runs to ExternalRef (externalRefType: documentation; locator: .gov/Regulaion-123; comment: An Passed Regulation). Three arrows labelled 'Contens' run from Regulation to Requirement (requirementText: Must provide a country of origin), Requirement (requirementText: Must provide a product name) and a stacked-document shape labelled 'Addition Requirements'. The spellings 'Contens', 'Regulaion' and 'Addition' are as drawn.",
